    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-027: @media Block Support** — @media block parsing + cascade-time viewport filtering. Third of the four-ADR arc (025→026→027→028) closing the parser gap that leaves Wikipedia's Vector-skin layout rules unreachable.\n\n**Documentation only.** Implementation (3 commits) lands in a follow-up PR.\n\n## Grounded in measurement\n\n### @media block census (Wikipedia CSS, 2026-10-25)\n\n| Query type | Blocks |\n|---|---|\n| `min-width` only | 24 |\n| `max-width` only | 18 |\n| Other (`screen`/`all`/compound) | 11 |\n| `prefers-color-scheme` | 5 |\n| `print` | 4 |\n| `prefers-reduced-motion` | 1 |\n| `min-width` + `max-width` combined | 1 |\n| **Total** | **64** |\n\n### Viewport-1024 firing analysis\n\n| Support level | Blocks firing | % |\n|---|---|---|\n| Without calc support | ~20 | 31% |\n| **With calc support** | **~33** | **52%** |\n\nThe 13-block delta is entirely `max-width: calc(1120px - 1px)` (= 1119) blocks — almost certainly the tablet mid-size layout rules. **Skipping calc would forfeit exactly the Vector-skin rules this ADR exists to reach.**\n\n### Content volume inside @media\n\n- 722 rules, 1,845 declarations\n- **953 consumed-property declarations (51.6%)** — properties our layout engine reads\n- **106 layout-property declarations (5.7%)** — grid/flex/column/float/position (which our layout engine currently ignores)\n\n### Vector skin class coverage inside @media\n\n| Class | Blocks |\n|---|---|\n| `.vector-menu` | 8 |\n| `.vector-header` | 7 |\n| `.vector-toc` | 5 |\n| `.vector-column-start` | 2 |\n| `.vector-body` | 1 |\n| `.vector-main-menu` | 1 |\n\n**The layout classes ADR-025 couldn't reach are confirmed to exist inside @media blocks.**\n\n## What the ADR specifies\n\n- **`MediaQuery` type**: unsupported flag + optional `min_width_px`/`max_width_px`.\n- **`Rule` gains `optional<MediaQuery> media`**: nullopt = unconditional rule.\n- **Prelude classifier**: `screen`/`all`/empty → always-match; `(min-width: Npx)` / `(max-width: Npx)` → width bounds; `calc(Npx ± Mpx)` → evaluated arithmetic; `and` combinations → both bounds; `print` / `prefers-*` / complex / mixed-unit-calc / range syntax → unsupported (rule dropped, correct per CSS spec).\n- **`cascade()` gains `viewport_width` param**: default 1024 for backward compat with all existing tests.\n- **`apply_rule()` early-returns** on media mismatch.\n- **`RenderPipeline::relayout`** passes viewport to cascade.\n\n## Why calc support in v1 (not deferred)\n\nThe `calc(1120px - 1px)` blocks are the tablet-layout rules. Without calc we skip them — losing exactly the payoff ADR-027 targets. Simple calc evaluation is ~30 lines for `Npx ± Mpx`, unlocks 13 firing blocks. Only `Npx ± Mpx` supported (covers 100% of Wikipedia's @media calc).\n\n## Meta-lesson-v3 caveat (built in from the start)\n\n**953 consumed-property declarations ≠ visible delta.**\n\nThe rule containing the declaration must ALSO win the cascade after gating passes, and the winning property must be one our layout engine consumes. **106 declarations target grid/flex/column — properties our layout engine ignores.**\n\nADR-027's visible delta is **measured in Commit 2, not predicted here**. If negligible (as ADR-026's var() was), ADR-027 is documented as **infrastructure for a future layout-engine ADR**.\n\nSame discipline that's run through ADR-023 → 024 → 025 → 026: predict from measured scale, trace the code path, verify cascade-winner, measure visible delta, document honestly.\n\n## The four-ADR arc\n\n| ADR | Status | Visible delta |\n|---|---|---|\n| **025** | merged | Article content styled (~40-50%) |\n| **026** | merged | Bug fix (display:none) + var() infra; **negligible var() delta** |\n| **027** | this PR | Uncertain — measured in Commit 2; may be infrastructure for grid/flex ADR |\n| **028** | after (`:not()` + attr-ops) | Unlocks remaining structural rules |\n\n## Reviewer checklist\n\n- [ ] **Calc support as v1 scope** — 30 lines to unlock 13 mid-size layout blocks. Comfortable with the tradeoff vs. shipping without and documenting the gap?\n- [ ] **Unsupported queries drop rules** — `print`/`prefers-*` rules never fire. Correct per CSS spec (browser without feature doesn't apply them). Agree?\n- [ ] **`viewport_width` as cascade param** (default 1024) — keeps `RenderState` focused on per-element state, matches `layout()`'s existing signature. No test breakage. Agree?\n- [ ] **Meta-lesson-v3 escape hatch** — 953 consumed declarations may still produce negligible visible delta. The ADR commits to measuring honestly in Commit 2. Comfortable with that commitment?\n- [ ] **Deferred scope** — print, prefers-color-scheme, prefers-reduced-motion, complex queries, range syntax, mixed-unit calc, nested @media, grid/flex layout. All reasonable for v1?\n\n## Deferred\n\n- Recursive `@media` (0 nested cases on Wikipedia)\n- `prefers-color-scheme`, `prefers-reduced-motion`, `prefers-contrast` (need OS/UI integration)\n- `@media print` (no print rendering yet)\n- Complex queries: `aspect-ratio`, `orientation`, `resolution`, `hover`, `pointer`, range syntax\n- `calc()` with mixed units (`calc(50% - 20px)`, `calc(10em + 2px)`)\n- Nested `@media` blocks\n- **Grid/flex/column layout engine** — the ADR that would fully unlock the Vector structural transform (106 layout declarations inside @media target these)\n\n## Test plan\n\nNo code touched, so no test changes. Will run `cmake --build build && ./build/tests/honeybee_tests` after merge to confirm `main` still clean (306 cases, 1297 assertions, unchanged).\n\n## ADR\n\n`docs/decisions/027-media-queries.md` — status Accepted; implementation in follow-up PR.\n\nRefs #156\n",
